    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129-a1">

                <pb facs="0244" n="898" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg898"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 213.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Belknap to Mr.
                            Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >War Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington
                                City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1875-04-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 7, 1875</date>. (Received April
                        9.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit, for your
                    information, copy of report of the commanding officer of Fort Duncan, Texas, of
                    depredations supposed to have been committed by Mexican Indians, including the
                    report of a scout, made by Lieutenant Markley Twenty-fourth Infantry, and map of
                    the country traveled over.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. W. BELKNAP.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
